  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The North Melbourne Kangaroos entered the 2026 AFLW grand final with the opportunity to achieve a rare three-peat, facing off against the Melbourne Demons. Following a competitive match at Ikon Park, North Melbourne secured the title with a 26-point win. The victory solidifies the club's dominance in the league, having now claimed three successive premierships. Club captain Jasmine Garner, who has been instrumental in the team's success, was awarded the best-on-ground medal for her performance. This achievement places Garner among a select group of athletes, as she is only the second player in the history of the AFLW to be awarded multiple grand final best-on-ground honors. While recent reports have focused on player movements and off-field issues at other clubs, the attention remains fixed on this historic achievement by the North Melbourne side.",
